A||N||8||85Josh||Car Died Today!||||8||
Z||000000||85Josh||04-22-2001||07:14 PM||||I was on my way to a friends house, and she just died a the light. No shakes, bangs, or smoke. I did notice that she seemed a little sluggish on the way, about 20 miles into the trip. As I tried to restart her, I go absolutly nothing when I turned the key, and the radio display slowly dimmed and died. The emergency flashers didn't work, either.<BR>Anyway, I think this sounds like a bad alternator, and was just looking for opinions as to whether you all agree or not. TIA<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||8
Z||000001||Spektyr||04-22-2001||07:16 PM||||My Lincoln did a similar thing... it had a bad diode in the alternator.  I could jumpstart it, but after I shut it off, it would stay dead.  The alternator had enough juice to run the car, but not charge the battery and run the car.<P>It's definitely charging system.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000002||85Josh||04-22-2001||07:24 PM||||Man, that was fast! I love this place! I plan on removing the alternator and battery tonight, and taking them to AutoZone for testing in the morning.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fldevel||04-23-2001||10:42 AM|||| check ur fuel pump too .. :P  haha .. uh inside joke i guess  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||04-23-2001||11:38 AM||||A few summers back I was driving across northern pennsylvania with the family in the full size dodge van we had. About an hour out the cruise control disengaged. I tried clicking it back on but it wouldnt engage anymore. I thought, "damn, the cruise control has failed"<P>about 30 miles down the road, just as we were cresting a hill the engine shut off. Same story as with your fiero, battery was almost competely dead. Had to replace the altenator. <P>If you charge the battery back up fully you should be able to drive it for an hour or two before it goes dead again (esp if you leave the lights, fans...off).<P>It turns out the cruise control was a kinda early warning that the battery voltage was dropping. It needed a higher voltage to run than the electronic ignition. (BTW the cruise control was fine once the altinator was replaced).||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||04-23-2001||11:47 AM||||When the alternator in my 88 went, the guage read 6, rather than 13, and I headed straight to the repair shop before the car battery died.  It alternator went while I was driving on the Daytona track no less.  I only had a couple of miles to the Firestone super store in Port Orange.||||reg||1
Z||000006||85Josh||04-23-2001||11:49 AM||||Thanks, Ken, I actually had the same thing happen in my fullsize 82 van. The cruise apparently needs at least 12 ful volts. That incident is what made me suspect the alternator. I just got it off the car(PITA), and am on my way to AutoZone to get it tested. By the way, don't follow the Haynes instructions to remove the alt! Just take out both of the mounting bolts, pull the wires and then remove the dogbone and it's mounting bracket. On the Duke, at least, this is the easiest way to go.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000007||85Josh||04-23-2001||10:10 PM||||Well, got the alternator back from AutoZone, they say the alternator tests good, but the battery has at least two cells shorted. Seems my rusted-out battery tray let the batt slide back and forth till it busted. Didn't have time to put it back together today, so I'll put the alternator and a new battery in her in the morning. Thanks for all the replies, I'll post the results.||||reg||1
Z||000008||85Josh||04-26-2001||10:10 AM||||SHE LIVES AGAIN! I went ahead and put in a new alternator, since close inspection revealed a lower mounting hole that was worn oblong, and I don't trust the cheap metal of these housings to survive. everything went well, once I figured out that I had to put the dogbone bolt in the engine side first, then in the back mount. Anyway, it runs just fine now.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||14
